<!-- ==========================================
     JAVA TOPICS
=========================================== -->

<h4 class="mt-4">

    🧠 Java Concepts

</h4>


<div class="accordion"
     id="javaTopics">


    <!-- BASIC PROGRAM -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#basicJava">

                1. Basic Java Program

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="basicJava"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Every Java application normally contains a
                <strong>main()</strong> method from which execution
                begins.

<pre>
class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        System.out.println("Hello World");

    }

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- VARIABLES -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#variables">

                2. Variables and Data Types

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="variables"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Variables are used to store data.

                <br><br>

                Common Java data types include:

                <ul>

                    <li>int – Integer values</li>

                    <li>float – Decimal values</li>

                    <li>double – Large decimal values</li>

                    <li>char – Single character</li>

                    <li>boolean – true or false</li>

                    <li>String – Sequence of characters</li>

                </ul>

<pre>
int age = 20;

double marks = 85.5;

char grade = 'A';

boolean passed = true;
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- OPERATORS -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#operators">

                3. Operators

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="operators"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Operators are used to perform operations
                on values.

                <br><br>

                Examples include:

                <ul>

                    <li>Arithmetic: +, -, *, /, %</li>

                    <li>Relational: &gt;, &lt;, ==, !=</li>

                    <li>Logical: &amp;&amp;, ||, !</li>

                </ul>

<pre>
int a = 10;
int b = 5;

System.out.println(a + b);
System.out.println(a - b);
System.out.println(a * b);
System.out.println(a / b);
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- IF ELSE -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#ifelse">

                4. If-Else

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="ifelse"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                If-else statements are used to make decisions.

<pre>
int age = 20;

if (age >= 18) {

    System.out.println("Eligible");

}
else {

    System.out.println("Not Eligible");

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- LOOP -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#loops">

                5. Loops

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="loops"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Loops are used to execute a block of code
                repeatedly.

<pre>
for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 5; i++) {

    System.out.println(i);

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- ARRAYS -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#arrays">

                6. Arrays

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="arrays"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                An array stores multiple values of the same
                data type.

<pre>
int numbers[] = {
    10, 20, 30, 40, 50
};

System.out.println(numbers[0]);
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- STRINGS -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#strings">

                7. Strings

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="strings"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Strings are used to store sequences of characters.

<pre>
String name = "Java";

System.out.println(name);

System.out.println(name.length());

System.out.println(name.toUpperCase());
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- METHODS -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#methods">

                8. Methods

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="methods"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Methods are blocks of code designed to perform
                a particular task.

<pre>
static int add(int a, int b) {

    return a + b;

}

public static void main(String[] args) {

    System.out.println(add(10, 20));

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- OOP -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#oops">

                9. Classes and Objects

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="oops"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                A class is a blueprint for creating objects.

                An object is an instance of a class.

<pre>
class Student {

    String name;

    void display() {

        System.out.println(name);

    }

}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Student s = new Student();

        s.name = "Manjiri";

        s.display();

    }

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- INHERITANCE -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#inheritance">

                10. Inheritance

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="inheritance"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Inheritance allows one class to acquire
                properties and methods of another class.

<pre>
class Animal {

    void sound() {

        System.out.println("Animal Sound");

    }

}

class Dog extends Animal {

    void bark() {

        System.out.println("Dog Barks");

    }

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- EXCEPTION -->

    <div class="accordion-item">

        <h2 class="accordion-header">

            <button
                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                data-bs-target="#exception">

                11. Exception Handling

            </button>

        </h2>

        <div id="exception"
             class="accordion-collapse collapse">

            <div class="accordion-body">

                Exception handling is used to handle runtime
                errors without terminating the program unexpectedly.

<pre>
try {

    int result = 10 / 0;

}
catch (ArithmeticException e) {

    System.out.println("Cannot divide by zero");

}
</pre>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</div>


